Explain this TLA-inspired RFS bounded buffer example:
```rfs
module bounded_buffer_tla {
  enum State { Empty, One, Full }
  initial Empty
  event Put
  event Get
  output BufferFull
  output BufferEmpty
  var count: bit<2> init 0
  transition Empty on Put { next One; set count = 1; }
  transition One on Put { next Full; set count = 2; emit BufferFull; }
  transition Full on Get { next One; set count = 1; }
  transition One on Get { next Empty; set count = 0; emit BufferEmpty; }
  prop state_matches_count : always ((state == Empty && count == 0) || (state == One && count == 1) || (state == Full && count == 2)) ;
}
```

Why does this TLA-inspired RFS attempt fail to parse?

```rfs
module bad_tla_prime {
  enum State { A }
  initial A
  event E
  var x: bit<8> init 0
  transition A on E {
    next A;
    set x = x';
  }
}
```

Why is this TLA-style RFS expression invalid?

```rfs
module bad_tla_set {
  enum State { A }
  initial A
  event E
  var x: bit<8> init 0
  transition A on E {
    next A;
    set x = {1, 2};
  }
}
```
